# Local time default (ALGR)

All Labs **web apps and sites** present and format times in the **viewer’s local timezone** unless the signed-in user (or prefs) has **explicitly selected a different timezone**.

## Default

- **Display / UI copy / relative labels** → device/browser local timezone (`Intl`, `Temporal`, or equivalent).
- **User preference timezone** → when set, use that IANA zone for that user’s views; do not invent a product-wide default zone.
- **No preference set** → stay on device local; do not fall back to UTC, “server time,” or a hard-coded region (e.g. `America/Denver`).

## Build & ops stamps

Version Refresh / `version.json` / build ids use the **build host’s local** offset (see skill `version-refresh`). That is host-local, not UTC `Z`.

## Storage & APIs

Keep **absolute instants** on the wire and in storage when that is idiomatic (e.g. UTC ISO for DB columns). Convert at the edge for display and for preference-TZ views. Do not store or show “naive” wall times as if they were UTC without an explicit product decision.

## Anti-patterns

| Avoid | Why |
|-------|-----|
| Defaulting UI to UTC `Z` | Users expect local wall time |
| `Date#toISOString()` for user-visible labels | Always UTC |
| Hard-coded product timezone with no pref | Wrong for multi-region / travel |
| Ignoring an explicit timezone preference | Preference is the override |
| Assuming “local” means the agent’s machine in client UI | Use the **viewer’s** environment |

## When implementing

1. Prefer existing app date helpers / prefs timezone if the product already has them.
2. New time UI: local first; wire preference TZ only when the product has (or is adding) that setting.
3. If a request would force UTC or a fixed zone into user-facing UI without a preference path — **stop and question** (pairs with challenge-best-practices / idiomatic-methodology).
